    # Publishes or updates a key in a map channel.
    #
    # The command making the call, checked as a Client checks it.
    #
    # @param channel [String, nil] The name of the map channel. Required.
    # @param key [String, nil] The entry key. Required.
    # @param data [Object, nil] The entry data. In the HTTP API it is any JSON value; over GRPC
    #   it may be binary.
    # @param b64data [String, nil] Data as base64, for binary over the HTTP API. Centrifugo
    #   decodes it.
    # @param stream_data [Object, nil] Currently not used by the server API.
    # @param b64stream_data [String, nil] Currently not used by the server API.
    # @param tags [Hash{String => String}] Key-value metadata attached to the publication.
    # @param idempotency_key [String, nil] Drops duplicate publications upon retries: a
    #   publication with a key already used in the channel is not applied
    #   again, and its result has the first one's position, with suppressed
    #   set and suppress_reason "idempotency". It acts per channel; keys are
    #   kept for 5 minutes by default. Every map broker - memory, Redis and
    #   PostgreSQL - keeps keys.
    # @param delta [Boolean, nil] Enables delta compression for this publication.
    # @param version [Integer, nil] A per-key version: publications with a version not higher
    #   than the key's current one are suppressed.
    # @param version_epoch [String, nil] Scopes version. A different epoch resets version
    #   comparison.
    # @param score [Integer, nil] Currently not used by the server API.
    # @param key_mode [String, nil] Makes the publish conditional: "if_new" writes only if the
    #   key does not exist, "if_exists" only if it exists. Empty always
    #   writes.
    # @return [Command]
    # @raise [InvalidRequestError]
